      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "quote",
      "text": "In 1886, Winslow Homer began to produce oil paintings and watercolors of subjects in the Adirondack Mountains, where he and his brother Charles had fished and hunted since the 1870s.",
      "source": {
        "author": "The Cleveland Museum of Art",
        "title": "Leaping Trout",
        "publisher": "The Cleveland Museum of Art",
        "readAt": "https://openaccess-api.clevelandart.org/api/artworks/147393",
        "accessed": "2026-11-03",
        "tier": 4,
        "license": "CC0"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind": "quote",
      "text": "The powerful Atlantic surf pounding against the desolate coast of Prouts Neck, Maine, provided primary subject matter for the dramatic paintings that Homer created during his final decades.",
      "source": {
